<title>JAPAN: Nippon TV hits record high in early Tokyo.</title>
<headline>Nippon TV hits record high in early Tokyo.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of nationwide broadcaster Nippon Television Network Corp rose to their highest level since the company's listing in 1959 in Tokyo morning trade on Monday, helped by news of Fuji Television Network Inc's planned listing on August 8, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0039 GMT, the shares stood at 49,000, up 600 yen from the Friday close, after briefly hitting a record high of 49,300. Turnover was 16,480 shares.</p>
